[{"page": 1, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-1", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "T1. A journey through time: The secrets of Avicenna", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 151.06434631347656, 469.6398620605469, 172.77197265625]}, {"text": "7%", "bbox": [290.6499938964844, 193.70750427246094, 304.6280822753906, 207.2747344970703]}, {"text": "1.1", "bbox": [195.72799682617188, 209.6475067138672, 209.79298400878906, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "1.2", "bbox": [227.35400390625, 209.6475067138672, 241.4189910888672, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "1.3", "bbox": [258.97998046875, 209.6475067138672, 273.0449523925781, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "1.4", "bbox": [290.60601806640625, 209.6475067138672, 304.6709899902344, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "1.5", "bbox": [322.23199462890625, 209.6475067138672, 336.2969665527344, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "1.6", "bbox": [353.8580017089844, 209.6475067138672, 367.9229736328125, 223.21473693847656]}, {"text": "∑", "bbox": [387.9630126953125, 194.75196838378906, 397.0688171386719, 229.34210205078125]}, {"text": "3", "bbox": [199.91200256347656, 225.5885009765625, 205.6083984375, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [231.53799438476562, 225.5885009765625, 237.23439025878906, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "3", "bbox": [263.16400146484375, 225.5885009765625, 268.8603820800781, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [294.78997802734375, 225.5885009765625, 300.4863586425781, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "7", "bbox": [326.416015625, 225.5885009765625, 332.1123962402344, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [358.0419921875, 225.5885009765625, 363.7383728027344, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "25", "bbox": [386.8190002441406, 225.5885009765625, 398.2139892578125, 239.15573120117188]}, {"text": "A chemist found herself in the 11 th Century, where she met the renowned physician Avicenna. In Avi-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 521.968505859375, 538.567138671875, 539.5206909179688]}, {"text": "cenna's laboratory, she discovered a blue elixir and a yellow mysterious stone. She brought them back", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 537.9085083007812, 538.5659790039062, 551.4757080078125]}, {"text": "to 2026. Determined to uncover their composition, she began her research.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 549.8644409179688, 409.9774169921875, 563.431640625]}, {"text": "Part 1. The blue elixir", "bbox": [56.29199981689453, 575.235595703125, 173.0382843017578, 590.1596069335938]}, {"text": "At first, the chemist compiled a table listing the names of the only four plants which she saw in Avicenna’s", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 594.2335205078125, 538.5841064453125, 607.8007202148438]}, {"text": "lab that could have been used to prepare the elixir, and the compounds that can be extracted from these", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 606.1885375976562, 538.5537109375, 619.7557373046875]}, {"text": "plants.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 618.1435546875, 88.17547607421875, 631.7107543945312]}]}, {"page": 2, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-2", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "Plants", "bbox": [105.25, 156.5345001220703, 133.96224975585938, 170.1017303466797]}, {"text": "Compounds that can be extracted", "bbox": [255.98899841308594, 156.5345001220703, 414.68548583984375, 170.1017303466797]}, {"text": "Zingiber", "bbox": [97.39800262451172, 187.30650329589844, 141.4370880126953, 200.8737335205078]}, {"text": "1 (C11H14O3)", "bbox": [192.0970001220703, 251.44650268554688, 254.94082641601562, 267.2128601074219]}, {"text": "2 (C10H18O)", "bbox": [317.13201904296875, 251.44650268554688, 374.3536682128906, 267.2128601074219]}, {"text": "3 (C10H18O)", "bbox": [428.75201416015625, 251.44650268554688, 485.97369384765625, 267.2128601074219]}, {"text": "Hypericum", "bbox": [94.29499816894531, 277.83551025390625, 144.91282653808594, 291.4027404785156]}, {"text": "4 (C6H12O)", "bbox": [197.47299194335938, 328.82550048828125, 249.567626953125, 344.59185791015625]}, {"text": "5 (C10H12O2)", "bbox": [314.32000732421875, 328.82550048828125, 377.1639099121094, 344.59185791015625]}, {"text": "6 (C10H18O)", "bbox": [428.75201416015625, 328.82550048828125, 485.97369384765625, 344.59185791015625]}, {"text": "Chamomilla", "bbox": [91.26399993896484, 362.3185119628906, 147.95358276367188, 375.8857421875]}, {"text": "7 (C14H16)", "bbox": [198.79800415039062, 434.6235046386719, 248.23883056640625, 450.3898620605469]}, {"text": "8 (C15H24)", "bbox": [321.02099609375, 434.6235046386719, 370.4618835449219, 450.3898620605469]}, {"text": "3 (C10H18O)", "bbox": [428.75201416015625, 434.6235046386719, 485.97369384765625, 450.3898620605469]}, {"text": "Artemisia", "bbox": [95.48600006103516, 467.04449462890625, 141.13702392578125, 480.6117248535156]}, {"text": "9 (C10H16O)", "bbox": [194.90899658203125, 536.1334838867188, 252.13063049316406, 551.89990234375]}, {"text": "10 (C10H18O)", "bbox": [314.28399658203125, 536.1334838867188, 377.20166015625, 551.89990234375]}, {"text": "3 (C10H18O)", "bbox": [428.75201416015625, 536.1334838867188, 485.97369384765625, 551.89990234375]}, {"text": "Using chromatography, she determined that the elixir consists of four different substances (X, Y, Z and", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 569.9645385742188, 538.5802612304688, 583.53173828125]}, {"text": "W).", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 581.9194946289062, 71.98444366455078, 595.4866943359375]}, {"text": "The chemist then discovered that X can isomerise into Y in an acidic medium and that Y has a plane of", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 599.8524780273438, 538.5731201171875, 613.419677734375]}, {"text": "symmetry.", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 611.8074951171875, 106.06832885742188, 625.3746948242188]}, {"text": "1.1", "bbox": [78.60802459716797, 634.7725219726562, 92.84236145019531, 648.3397216796875]}, {"text": "Identify X and Y.", "bbox": [114.69256591796875, 634.7725219726562, 195.36964416503906, 648.3397216796875]}, {"text": "3.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 634.696533203125, 521.8194580078125, 648.2637329101562]}]}, {"page": 3, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-3", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "Chromatography also revealed it was substance Z that gave the elixir its blue colour. Z is a derivative", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.5823974609375, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "of the well-known substance A, which has two perpendicular planes of symmetry. When heated, A iso-", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 167.17449951171875, 538.5845336914062, 180.74172973632812]}, {"text": "merises into aromatic compound B, which has three mutually perpendicular planes of symmetry. When", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 179.12950134277344, 538.5634155273438, 192.6967315673828]}, {"text": "substance Z is chlorinated, a pair of peaks with an intensity ratio of 3:1 is observed in the mass spectrum", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 191.0854949951172, 538.5729370117188, 204.65272521972656]}, {"text": "at m/z 218 and 220, respectively.", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 203.04049682617188, 209.1712188720703, 216.60772705078125]}, {"text": "1.2", "bbox": [78.60796356201172, 226.0054931640625, 92.84230041503906, 239.57272338867188]}, {"text": "Identify Z and draw the structures of substances A and B.", "bbox": [114.6925048828125, 226.0054931640625, 387.8756103515625, 239.57273864746094]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.4499816894531, 225.92950439453125, 521.8193969726562, 239.49673461914062]}, {"text": "The chemist extracted W from the elixir. When W was added to an aqueous Fe3+ solution, a charac-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 242.63922119140625, 538.5848999023438, 273.77056884765625]}, {"text": "teristic colour change was observed. Mass spectrometric analysis of W revealed the intensity ratio of", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 270.93951416015625, 538.5868530273438, 284.5067443847656]}, {"text": "[M]+ ∶[M + 1]+= 9:1, where M is the molecular ion. Assume carbon consists exclusively of 12C and 13C,", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 259.55712890625, 538.583984375, 325.5095520019531]}, {"text": "the natural isotopic abundance of 12C is 98.9%, and all other elements are monoisotopic.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 281.4671936035156, 470.72039794921875, 316.58355712890625]}, {"text": "1.3", "bbox": [78.60798645019531, 320.7764892578125, 92.84232330322266, 334.3437194824219]}, {"text": "Determine the number of carbon atoms (𝑛) from the mass spec data and", "bbox": [114.6925277709961, 305.8609619140625, 480.5740966796875, 340.45111083984375]}, {"text": "identify W. Show your calculations.", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 332.73248291015625, 281.8526306152344, 346.29974365234375]}, {"text": "3.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 320.7015075683594, 521.8194580078125, 334.26873779296875]}, {"text": "Part 2. The mysterious stone", "bbox": [56.29199981689453, 373.14959716796875, 213.35301208496094, 388.0736083984375]}, {"text": "Avicenna had told her the stone was a stoichiometric compound. She dissolved it in dilute nitric acid.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 392.1474914550781, 538.5855712890625, 405.7147216796875]}, {"text": "After that, she adjusted the pH of the solution to ~4 and added NaF. This led to the formation of pre-", "bbox": [56.69300842285156, 404.10247802734375, 538.5619506835938, 417.6697082519531]}, {"text": "cipitate C ⋅𝑥H2O, which contained 39.16% water by mass. Anhydrous C reacts with an excess of NaF to", "bbox": [56.69300842285156, 401.1419372558594, 538.5809936523438, 435.7320861816406]}, {"text": "yield compound D, which contains 32.85% sodium and 12.85% of metal Q by mass, and is used in the", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 428.012451171875, 538.57373046875, 441.5796813964844]}, {"text": "industrial production of Q.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 439.9674377441406, 180.75863647460938, 453.53466796875]}, {"text": "1.4", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 553.6044921875, 92.84233856201172, 567.1716918945312]}, {"text": "Identify metal Q and compounds C ⋅𝑥H2O and D.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 538.68896484375, 348.12060546875, 573.2791137695312]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.4499816894531, 553.5294799804688, 521.8193969726562, 567.0966796875]}, {"text": "Avicenna told her that he found the stone in a coal deposit. The stone contains the anion of a highly", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 586.58349609375, 538.5711059570312, 600.1506958007812]}, {"text": "symmetrical acid F. Reaction of F with P2O5 gives binary compound G, which contains 49.98% of oxygen", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 598.5385131835938, 538.5921630859375, 614.5967407226562]}, {"text": "by mass and has a three-fold symmetry axis. F can be prepared by oxidising compound E with potassium", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 610.4935302734375, 538.5803833007812, 624.0607299804688]}, {"text": "permanganate in an acidic solution. E contains 11.18% of hydrogen by mass and has a six-fold symmetry", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 622.4485473632812, 538.5767822265625, 636.0157470703125]}, {"text": "axis.", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 634.403564453125, 77.56526947021484, 647.9707641601562]}, {"text": "1.5", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 732.7954711914062, 92.84233856201172, 746.3626708984375]}, {"text": "Draw the structures of E, F, and G.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 732.7954711914062, 276.1466064453125, 746.3626708984375]}, {"text": "7.0 pt", "bbox": [495.4499816894531, 732.720458984375, 521.8193969726562, 746.2876586914062]}, {"text": "Then, she analysed the stone thermogravimetrically in open air. A 10.00 g sample began to lose mass", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 748.56298828125, 538.5748291015625, 783.1531372070312]}]}, {"page": 4, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-4", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "at approximately 100 ∘C and stopped at 5.75 g at 200 ∘C. A second drop in mass was observed at 400 ∘C,", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 130.40113830566406, 538.5826416015625, 196.35354614257812]}, {"text": "with a final mass of 1.50 g of compound H remaining constant at higher temperatures.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 167.17449951171875, 462.03106689453125, 180.74172973632812]}, {"text": "1.6", "bbox": [78.60798645019531, 190.1405029296875, 92.84232330322266, 203.70773315429688]}, {"text": "Determine the chemical formulae of the stone and compound H using ther-", "bbox": [114.6925277709961, 190.1405029296875, 480.5766906738281, 203.70773315429688]}, {"text": "mogravimetric data.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 202.0955047607422, 209.55555725097656, 215.66273498535156]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 190.0644989013672, 521.8194580078125, 203.63172912597656]}]}]